1
00:05:26,666 --> 00:05:32,666
Geek Charming is a comedy, drama, family film directed by Jeffrey Hornaday.

2
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:59,333
Film geek Josh is looking for the subject of his new documentary when a chance meeting
puts the perfect star in his sights—Dylan, his school's most popular junior.

3
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:26,000
But Dylan's hopes of using the film to become Blossom Queen don't quite match
with Josh's goal to make a hard-hitting exposé about popularity.

4
00:21:46,666 --> 00:21:52,666
Will Josh shoot the film as planned, or show Dylan as
the truly interesting person she is?

5
00:27:13,333 --> 00:27:19,333
Dylan Schoenfield, played by Sarah Hyland.

6
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Josh Rosen, played by Matt Prokop.

7
00:38:06,666 --> 00:38:12,666
Hannah, played by Vanessa Morgan.

8
00:43:33,333 --> 00:43:39,333
Amy Loubalu, played by Sasha Pieterse.

9
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Lola, played by Lili Simmons.

10
00:54:26,666 --> 00:54:32,666
Nicole Paterson, played by Andrea Brooks.

11
00:59:53,333 --> 00:59:59,333
Geek Charming is a 2011 American teen comedy-drama film
released as a Disney Channel Original Movie.

12
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
It was directed by Jeffrey Hornaday from a screenplay by Elizabeth Hackett and
Hilary Galanoy, and based on the novel of the same name by Robin Palmer.

13
01:10:46,666 --> 01:10:52,666
The film stars Sarah Hyland and Matt Prokop.

14
01:16:13,333 --> 01:16:19,333
It premiered on November 11, 2011, on Disney Channel, on January 27, 2012, on Disney
Channel (UK & Ireland), and on January 28, 2012, on Disney Channel Asia.

15
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:46,000
The premiere was watched by 4.9 million viewers, the fifth
largest number for a cable show of that week.

16
01:27:06,666 --> 01:27:12,666
The film explores themes of high school, based on novel or book,
unlikely lovers, documentary filmmaking, teenage romance.

17
01:32:33,333 --> 01:32:39,333
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
